===Etymology===
Originally "The Bailey", a street running outside the western wall of medieval London; from the word {{m|en|bailey}}, a Middle English term for the outermost wall or court of a fortification. The courthouse built nearby in the 16th century, alongside old {{w|Newgate Prison}}, took its name from the street.

